Rule 1 (no complex dtypes for tensor–tensor operands)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 9 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 10 ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≠ 9 ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≠ 10
>>
Rule 3 (tensor–tensor shapes must match exactly to avoid size mismatch)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 5 (out must be a bool tensor and match inputs’ shape for tensor–tensor)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_3) = 0 ∧ ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) ∧ shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_1, i)
